  "narrative": "Compared to the last sale (September 10, 2026): No market trend is available for feeder cattle due to limited comparable receipts, however, a lower undertone was noted for feeder steer classes and a higher undertone was noted for feeder heifers and bulls. Quality this week was mixed. Calves offered plain to average quality and yearlings offered average to attractive quality. Demand was mostly moderate to good for light offerings. Weigh up cows sold on mostly light to moderate demand and offerings. Cow quality was mostly plain to average today. Feeding cows sold mostly 3.00 to 5.00 lower. Slaughter cows sold generally steady to 4.00 lower on all offerings. Slaughter bulls sold mostly 4.00 to 6.00 higher. Young age cow offerings were too lightly tested to develop any market trend. Supply included: 73% Feeder Cattle (37% Steers, 58% Heifers, 5% Bulls); 21% Slaughter Cattle (56% Cows, 44% Bulls); 6% Replacement Cattle (74% Stock Cows, 20% Bred Cows, 7% Cow-Calf Pairs). Feeder cattle supply over 600 lbs was 47%.",
